IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei7-related-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23): RELATED PROVISIONS of amending Acts of 2003 to 2010 (src:3599-3692).
-- Written by piece ei7 (Sonnet 5.5). Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; nothing here claims to be verified against the official text.
-- Seat: the person who has lost work or cannot work, or is self-employed, asking which law governs their claim.
--
-- What these provisions are. Each is a transitional or savings provision of an amending Act, shown by the
-- consolidation "for information". Most say from which day, or for which benefit period or week, an amendment
-- applies. The amendments themselves are not here: the text of the Act in force is encoded by the other pieces, and
-- a rule below only says whether the amendment reaches the person's benefit period or week.
-- A day that an amending Act fixes by "the day on which this Act comes into force" or "receives royal assent", or
-- that an order fixes, is not in the deposited texts: each is a DATE input of the rule that needs it, with a comment.
-- A day that the text itself states is a named constant with an @ref, defined once.
-- Rule names begin "Act RP": related provision of the Act.

§ `2003, c. 15, s. 25(1) - application of sections 15 to 20 and 22`

-- (a) a benefit period that begins on or after the day: every week of it is covered. (b) a benefit period that has
-- not ended before the day: only the weeks that begin on or after the day. "Has not ended before" is read as the
-- last day of the benefit period being the day or later (fork F1: the last day counts as part of the benefit period; every
-- gate below that says "has not ended before" is read the same way).
-- src:3601 | — 2003, c. 15, s. 25(1)
-- src:3602 | 25 (1) Sections 15 to 20 and 22 apply to a claimant for any benefit period
-- src:3603 | (a) that begins on or after January 4, 2004; or
-- src:3604 | (b) that has not ended before January 4, 2004, but only for weeks of benefits that begin on or after that date.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2003, c. 15, s. 25(1)(a), (b) (src:3603-3604)
`Act RP 2003 c. 15 s. 25(1) January 4, 2004` MEANS YearMonthDay 2004 1 4

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2003, c. 15, s. 25(1) (src:3602-3604)
GIVEN `the benefit period` IS A `Period of days`  -- out of range: section 9 and 10, benefit period (piece ei1); sections 152.1 and 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
      `the first day of the week of benefits` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2003 c. 15 s. 25(1) sections 15 to 20 and 22 apply to the week of benefits` IF
        `the benefit period`'s `first day of the period` AT LEAST `Act RP 2003 c. 15 s. 25(1) January 4, 2004`
    OR  (    `the benefit period`'s `last day of the period` AT LEAST `Act RP 2003 c. 15 s. 25(1) January 4, 2004`
         AND `the first day of the week of benefits` AT LEAST `Act RP 2003 c. 15 s. 25(1) January 4, 2004`)

§ `2005, c. 34, s. 56 - repeal of sections 127 and 128`

-- A saving: the repeal does not affect the validity of a disclosure or agreement made under the repealed sections by
-- either Minister named. "Does not affect" leaves the validity it had when made, so the rule returns that and
-- nothing for anything the saving does not name.
-- src:3606 | — 2005, c. 34, s. 56
-- src:3607 | Repeal of sections 127 and 128 of the Employment Insurance Act
-- src:3608 | 56 The repeal of sections 127 and 128 of the Employment Insurance Act does not affect the validity of a disclosure of information, or an agreement for the purpose of making information available, made under those sections by the Minister of Human Resources Development or the Minister of State to be styled Minister of Human Resources and Skills Development.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2005, c. 34, s. 56 (src:3608)
GIVEN `a disclosure of information, or an agreement for the purpose of making information available, was made under section 127 or 128` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made by the Minister of Human Resources Development or the Minister of State to be styled Minister of Human Resources and Skills Development` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was valid when it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2005 c. 34 s. 56 the validity of a disclosure or agreement made under the repealed sections 127 and 128` IS
    IF `a disclosure of information, or an agreement for the purpose of making information available, was made under section 127 or 128`
       AND `it was made by the Minister of Human Resources Development or the Minister of State to be styled Minister of Human Resources and Skills Development`
    THEN JUST `it was valid when it was made`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `2008, c. 28, s. 39(3), (4) - application to remittances`

-- Both subsections look at a day "after February 25, 2008". A remittance first due on that day itself is outside.
-- src:3610 | — 2008, c. 28, ss. 39(3), (4)
-- src:3611 | 39 (3) Subsection (1) applies in respect of remittances by a prescribed person that are first due after February 25, 2008.
-- src:3612 | (4) Subsection (2) applies in respect of payments and remittances that are required to be first made after February 25, 2008.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2008, c. 28, s. 39(3), (4) (src:3611-3612)
`Act RP 2008 c. 28 s. 39 February 25, 2008` MEANS YearMonthDay 2008 2 25

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2008, c. 28, s. 39(3) (src:3611)
GIVEN `the remittance is by a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: Part IV, remittances (piece ei3)
      `the day on which the remittance was first due` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2008 c. 28 s. 39(3) subsection (1) applies to the remittance` IF
        `the remittance is by a prescribed person`
    AND `the day on which the remittance was first due` GREATER THAN `Act RP 2008 c. 28 s. 39 February 25, 2008`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2008, c. 28, s. 39(4) (src:3612)
GIVEN `the day on which the payment or remittance is required to be first made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2008 c. 28 s. 39(4) subsection (2) applies to the payment or remittance` IF
    `the day on which the payment or remittance is required to be first made` GREATER THAN `Act RP 2008 c. 28 s. 39 February 25, 2008`

§ `2009, c. 2, s. 226(2) - Pilot Project No. 10`

-- The second Sunday before a day: the first Sunday before is the Sunday that begins the week containing the day
-- before the day (so a day that is itself a Sunday has the Sunday a week earlier as its first); the second is a
-- week before that. Fork F2: the text does not say whether "before the day" excludes the day itself.
-- src:3618 | — 2009, c. 2, s. 226(2)
-- src:3619 | Transitional
-- src:3620 | 226 (2) The maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period that is established for a claimant who is included in Pilot Project No. 10 and whose benefit period has not ended before the second Sunday before the day on which this Act receives royal assent is to be determined in accordance with Schedule I to the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by subsection 224(1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 2, s. 226(2) (src:3620)
GIVEN `the day on which the 2009 Act receives royal assent` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 226(2) the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` IS
    (`s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` (`the day on which the 2009 Act receives royal assent` MINUS 1)) MINUS 7

-- The rule says only which Schedule I governs: Schedule I "as enacted by subsection 224(1)" is not in the deposited
-- text (the Schedule I of the Act in force is another piece's), so the maximum number of weeks is not worked out here.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 2, s. 226(2) (src:3620)
GIVEN `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 10` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: regulation 77.6, Pilot Project No. 10 (piece er5)
      `the benefit period` IS A `Period of days`  -- out of range: section 9 and 10, benefit period (piece ei1); sections 152.1 and 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
      `the day on which the 2009 Act receives royal assent` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 226(2) the maximum number of weeks is determined under Schedule I as enacted by subsection 224(1)` IF
        `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 10`
    AND `the benefit period`'s `last day of the period` AT LEAST `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 226(2) the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` `the day on which the 2009 Act receives royal assent`

§ `2009, c. 2, ss. 227 and 228 - premium rates deemed for 2002, 2003 and 2005`

-- Each section deems a section of the Act (66.1, 66.3) to have read as quoted. The deemed section fixes a premium
-- rate "notwithstanding section 66" (the general rate-setting section, another piece's), so for a year it names the
-- rate is the one stated and for any other year the text says nothing: NOTHING, and section 66 governs.
-- "respectively": 2002 pairs with 2.2% and 2003 with 2.1%.
-- src:3622 | — 2009, c. 2, s. 227
-- src:3623 | Deeming provision
-- src:3624 | 227 Section 66.1 of the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by section 9 of chapter 5 of the Statutes of Canada, 2001, is deemed to have read as follows:
-- src:3625 | Premium rates for 2002 and 200366.1Notwithstanding section 66, the premium rates for the years 2002 and 2003 are 2.2% and 2.1%, respectively.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 2, s. 227 (src:3625)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 227 the premium rate for the year deemed by section 66.1` IS
    BRANCH IF year EQUALS 2002 THEN JUST (2.2%)
           IF year EQUALS 2003 THEN JUST (2.1%)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:3627 | — 2009, c. 2, s. 228
-- src:3628 | Deeming provision
-- src:3629 | 228 Section 66.3 of the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by section 25 of chapter 22 of the Statutes of Canada, 2004, is deemed to have read as follows:
-- src:3630 | Premium rate for 200566.3Notwithstanding section 66, the premium rate for the year 2005 is 1.95%.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 2, s. 228 (src:3630)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 228 the premium rate for the year deemed by section 66.3` IS
    IF year EQUALS 2005 THEN JUST (1.95%) ELSE NOTHING

§ `2009, c. 2, s. 229 - application of subsection 224(1)`

-- "Has not ended before the day": the last day of the benefit period is the day or later. "Does not begin after
-- September 11, 2010": the first day is that day or earlier.
-- src:3632 | — 2009, c. 2, s. 229
-- src:3633 | Application
-- src:3634 | 229 Subsection 224(1) applies with respect to every claimant whose benefit period has not ended before the day on which that subsection comes into force and whose benefit period does not begin after September 11, 2010.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 2, s. 229 (src:3634)
`Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 229 September 11, 2010` MEANS YearMonthDay 2010 9 11

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 2, s. 229 (src:3634)
GIVEN `the benefit period` IS A `Period of days`  -- out of range: section 9 and 10, benefit period (piece ei1); sections 152.1 and 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
      `the day on which subsection 224(1) comes into force` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 229 subsection 224(1) applies to the claimant` IF
        `the benefit period`'s `last day of the period` AT LEAST `the day on which subsection 224(1) comes into force`
    AND `the benefit period`'s `first day of the period` AT MOST `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 229 September 11, 2010`

§ `2009, c. 30, s. 7 - subsection 55(10) of the Regulations`

-- The section deems subsection 55(10) of the Employment Insurance Regulations to read as quoted, for a claimant to whom
-- any of sections 3 to 6 of the 2009 Act applies and whose benefit period has not been extended under any of
-- subsections 10(13) to (13.3). The same section is shown in the Regulations' file (SOR-96-332.txt, src:2467-2470),
-- which piece er6 encodes; the names here begin "Act RP" so the two cannot clash.
-- src:3636 | — 2009, c. 30, s. 7
-- src:3637 | Subsection 55(10) of regulations
-- src:3638 | 7 With respect to a claimant to whom any of sections 3 to 6 applies whose benefit period has not been extended under any of subsections 10(13) to (13.3) of the Employment Insurance Act, subsection 55(10) of the Employment Insurance Regulations is deemed to read as follows:
-- src:3639 | (10)In a claimant’s benefit period, a claimant who is not in Canada or a claimant referred to in subsection (8), subject to the applicable maximums set out in paragraphs (7)(a) and (b), may combine the weeks of benefits to which the claimant is entitled, but the total number of weeks of benefits shall not exceed 50 or, if the maximum number of weeks during which benefits may be paid to a claimant under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 is equal to or greater than 50 weeks as a result of the application of any provision of any Act of Parliament, other than the Employment Insurance Act, the number that corresponds to that maximum number of weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 30, s. 7 (src:3638)
GIVEN `any of sections 3 to 6 of the 2009 Act applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: sections 3 to 6 of 2009, c. 30; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
      `the claimant's benefit period has been extended under any of subsections 10(13) to (13.3)` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 10(13) to (13.3), extension of the benefit period (piece ei1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 subsection 55(10) of the Regulations is deemed to read as set out in this section` IF
        `any of sections 3 to 6 of the 2009 Act applies to the claimant`
    AND (NOT `the claimant's benefit period has been extended under any of subsections 10(13) to (13.3)`)

-- "the total number of weeks of benefits shall not exceed 50 or, if the maximum number of weeks ... under section 225
-- of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 is equal to or greater than 50 weeks as a result of the application of any
-- provision of any Act of Parliament, other than the Employment Insurance Act, the number that corresponds to that
-- maximum number of weeks."
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 30, s. 7 (src:3639)
GIVEN `the maximum number of weeks under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009, as a result of a provision of an Act other than the Employment Insurance Act` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the most weeks of benefits that may be paid in total when weeks are combined` IS
    IF `the maximum number of weeks under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009, as a result of a provision of an Act other than the Employment Insurance Act` AT LEAST 50
    THEN `the maximum number of weeks under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009, as a result of a provision of an Act other than the Employment Insurance Act`
    ELSE 50

-- "a claimant who is not in Canada or a claimant referred to in subsection (8), subject to the applicable maximums
-- set out in paragraphs (7)(a) and (b), may combine the weeks of benefits to which the claimant is entitled, but the
-- total ... shall not exceed" the cap. Both limits bind, so the lesser of the weeks entitled, the applicable
-- maximum under (7)(a) and (b) and the cap is the most that can be paid. Fork F3.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 30, s. 7 (src:3639)
GIVEN `any of sections 3 to 6 of the 2009 Act applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: sections 3 to 6 of 2009, c. 30; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
      `the claimant's benefit period has been extended under any of subsections 10(13) to (13.3)` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 10(13) to (13.3), extension of the benefit period (piece ei1)
      `the claimant is not in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is referred to in subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: regulation 55(8) (piece er3)
      `the weeks of benefits to which the claimant is entitled` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 12, maximum number of weeks (piece ei1)
      `the applicable maximum set out in paragraphs (7)(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: regulation 55(7)(a) and (b) (piece er3)
      `the maximum number of weeks under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009, as a result of a provision of an Act other than the Employment Insurance Act` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the total number of weeks of benefits that the claimant may combine` IS
    IF     `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 subsection 55(10) of the Regulations is deemed to read as set out in this section` `any of sections 3 to 6 of the 2009 Act applies to the claimant` `the claimant's benefit period has been extended under any of subsections 10(13) to (13.3)`
       AND (`the claimant is not in Canada` OR `the claimant is referred to in subsection (8)`)
    THEN JUST (min `the weeks of benefits to which the claimant is entitled` (min `the applicable maximum set out in paragraphs (7)(a) and (b)` (`Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the most weeks of benefits that may be paid in total when weeks are combined` `the maximum number of weeks under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009, as a result of a provision of an Act other than the Employment Insurance Act`)))
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `2009, c. 33, ss. 18 to 20 - self-employed persons`

-- s. 18: an agreement under subsection 152.02(1) may be entered into from the day the 2009 Act receives royal
-- assent to the day section 16 comes into force, both days included; one entered into in that period is deemed to
-- have been entered into on the day section 16 comes into force.
-- src:3641 | — 2009, c. 33, s. 18
-- src:3642 | Agreements
-- src:3643 | 18 Agreements referred to in subsection 152.02(1) of the Employment Insurance Act may be entered into at any time during the period that begins on the day on which this Act receives royal assent and ends on the day on which section 16 comes into force, but any such agreement that is entered into during that period is deemed to have been entered into on the day on which that section comes into force.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 33, s. 18 (src:3643)
GIVEN `the day on which the agreement is entered into` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the 2009 Act receives royal assent` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
      `the day on which section 16 comes into force` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 18 an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1) may be entered into on the day` IF
        `the day on which the agreement is entered into` AT LEAST `the day on which the 2009 Act receives royal assent`
    AND `the day on which the agreement is entered into` AT MOST `the day on which section 16 comes into force`

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 33, s. 18 (src:3643)
GIVEN `the day on which the agreement is entered into` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the 2009 Act receives royal assent` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
      `the day on which section 16 comes into force` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 18 the day on which the agreement is deemed to have been entered into` IS
    IF `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 18 an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1) may be entered into on the day` `the day on which the agreement is entered into` `the day on which the 2009 Act receives royal assent` `the day on which section 16 comes into force`
    THEN JUST `the day on which section 16 comes into force`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s. 19: despite paragraph 152.07(1)(a), a Part VII.1 benefit period may begin on or after January 1, 2011 if the
-- self-employed person entered into the agreement in the period that begins on the later of the royal assent day
-- and January 1, 2010 and ends on April 1, 2010.
-- src:3645 | — 2009, c. 33, s. 19
-- src:3646 | Benefit periods during 2011
-- src:3647 | 19 Despite paragraph 152.07(1)(a) of the Employment Insurance Act, a benefit period under Part VII.1 of that Act may begin on or after January 1, 2011 if the self-employed person to whom the benefit period relates has, during the period that begins on the later of the day on which this Act receives royal assent and January 1, 2010 and ends on April 1, 2010, entered into an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1) of that Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 33, s. 19 (src:3647)
`Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 January 1, 2010` MEANS YearMonthDay 2010 1 1

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 33, s. 19 (src:3647)
`Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 April 1, 2010` MEANS YearMonthDay 2010 4 1

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 33, s. 19 (src:3647)
`Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 January 1, 2011` MEANS YearMonthDay 2011 1 1

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 33, s. 19 (src:3647)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE  -- out of range: section 10(1), the day a benefit period begins (piece ei1); section 152.11 for a self-employed person (piece ei5)
      `the day on which the self-employed person entered into an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1)` IS A DATE  -- out of range: section 152.02(1), the agreement with the Commission (piece ei5)
      `the day on which the 2009 Act receives royal assent` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 a benefit period under Part VII.1 may begin on or after January 1, 2011` IF
        `the first day of the benefit period` AT LEAST `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 January 1, 2011`
    AND `the day on which the self-employed person entered into an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1)` AT MOST `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 April 1, 2010`
    AND `the day on which the self-employed person entered into an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1)` AT LEAST
        (IF `the day on which the 2009 Act receives royal assent` AT LEAST `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 January 1, 2010`
         THEN `the day on which the 2009 Act receives royal assent`
         ELSE `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 January 1, 2010`)

-- s. 20: a violation accumulated under section 7.1 before subsection 152.07(6) came into force is deemed to be a
-- violation accumulated under section 152.07 on the day the notice of violation was given.
-- src:3649 | — 2009, c. 33, s. 20
-- src:3650 | Violations
-- src:3651 | 20 For the purpose of subsection 152.07(6) of the Employment Insurance Act, a violation accumulated by an individual under section 7.1 of that Act before the coming into force of that subsection is deemed to be a violation accumulated by the individual under section 152.07 on the day on which the notice of violation was given to the individual even though that section was not in force on that day.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2009, c. 33, s. 20 (src:3651)
GIVEN `the violation was accumulated under section 7.1 before the coming into force of subsection 152.07(6)` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 7.1, violations (piece ei1)
      `the day on which the notice of violation was given to the individual` IS A DATE  -- out of range: section 7.1, notice of violation (piece ei1)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 20 the day on which the violation is deemed to have been accumulated under section 152.07` IS
    IF `the violation was accumulated under section 7.1 before the coming into force of subsection 152.07(6)`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the notice of violation was given to the individual`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `2010, c. 9, s. 4 - parental leave deferred or returned to duty under the National Defence Act`

-- A benefit period or a period under subsection 23(2) extended "to 104 weeks" is read as 104 weeks of seven days
-- counted from its first day, the first day included, so its last day is the first day plus 104 x 7 - 1.
-- "Less than 104 weeks before the day" is read as fewer than 728 days and at least one day before it. Fork F4.
-- src:3653 | — 2010, c. 9, s. 4
-- src:3654 | Transitional
-- src:3655 | 4 (1) Sections 2 and 3 apply to a claimant whose benefit period began less than 104 weeks before the day on which this Act comes into force if the period referred to in subsection 23(2) of the Employment Insurance Act
-- src:3656 | (a) has not ended before that day; or
-- src:3657 | (b) ended before that day and, within the period referred to in that subsection, the claimant’s parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty from parental leave in accordance with regulations made under the National Defence Act, and the claimant’s deferral or return to duty, as the case may be, has not ended before that day.
-- src:3658 | Special case
-- src:3659 | (2) Section 2 applies to a claimant and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) of the Employment Insurance Act is extended to 104 weeks if
-- src:3660 | (a) within the period referred to in that subsection, in accordance with regulations made under the National Defence Act, the claimant’s parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty from parental leave, as the case may be;
-- src:3661 | (b) the claimant’s deferral or return to duty ended before the day on which this Act comes into force;
-- src:3662 | (c) the claimant’s benefit period has not ended before that day; and
-- src:3663 | (d) the period referred to in that subsection ended before that day.
-- src:3664 | Other special case
-- src:3665 | (3) A claimant’s benefit period and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) of the Employment Insurance Act are each extended to 104 weeks if
-- src:3666 | (a) within the period referred to in that subsection, in accordance with regulations made under the National Defence Act, the claimant’s parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty from parental leave, as the case may be;
-- src:3667 | (b) the claimant’s deferral or return to duty ended before the day on which this Act comes into force; and
-- src:3668 | (c) the claimant’s benefit period and the period referred to in that subsection each began less than 104 weeks before that day and both ended before that day.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2010, c. 9, s. 4(1), (2), (3) (src:3655) (src:3659) (src:3665)
`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4 104 weeks` MEANS 104

@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provision of 2010, c. 9, s. 4 (src:3655-3668)
GIVEN `the first day of a benefit period or of the period referred to in subsection 23(2)` IS A DATE  -- out of range: sections 10 and 23(2) (piece ei1)
      `the day on which the 2010 Act comes into force` IS A DATE  -- out of range: the amending Act's own commencement or royal assent; not in the deposited texts (no piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4 the period began less than 104 weeks before the day on which the Act comes into force` IF
        `the first day of a benefit period or of the period referred to in subsection 23(2)` LESS THAN `the day on which the 2010 Act comes into force`
    AND (Day `the day on which the 2010 Act comes into force` MINUS Day `the first day of a benefit period or of the period referred to in subsection 23(2)`) LESS THAN (`weeks as days` `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4 104 weeks`)

